<section class="about-site">
  <p class="label">What this site is</p>
  <p>
    This is my public notebook. I learn by building and explaining, and
    everything that produces ends up here, in four shapes.
  </p>
  <p>
    The <strong>blog</strong> holds long-form series you read like chapters, the
    biggest being the mathematics ML runs on, built from the silicon up. The
    <strong>courses</strong> section carries the slides and material from courses
    I teach, like computer organisation and design. <strong>Projects</strong> is
    the maker log: embedded systems, TinyML experiments, things that worked and
    things that did not. <strong>Papers</strong> is the newest thread, short
    honest reviews of what I am reading. And <strong>Culti7</strong> is the one
    finished thing among all the works-in-progress: a moisture meter for cashew
    processors that has been in the field since 2021.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most of this is in progress. Some of it is wrong on the first try. I fix it
    as I learn better. If you work on similar things, I would genuinely love to
    hear from you.
  </p>
</section>
